{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"syllabic-spiteful-urutu","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The remedy the error offers cannot satisfy a non-completion close\n\n`close_precheck` already supports closing a bug as `duplicate` / `not_a_bug` /\n`escalated` without fix evidence: when `close_class` is in\n`_NON_COMPLETION_BUG_CLASSES` **and** `_has_live_replacement_link()` finds a live\nreplacement, it routes to `close_disposition.verdict()` instead of the completion\nverifier.\n\n`_has_live_replacement_link` reads reduced-state `deps` for a `duplicates` relation. A\nticket whose description NAMES its canonical ticket in prose — but carries no link — has\n`deps == []`, so the precheck silently falls through to the ordinary completion verifier.\n\n## Why the fallthrough is actively misleading\nThe verifier then synthesizes 'Bug <title> is actually resolved' from the title and fails\nit, which is CORRECT on the facts (a duplicate's defect is not resolved by the duplicate).\nBut the remediation text it prints offers only two paths:\n  1. 'complete any unfinished work and make its proof discoverable' — impossible; the work\n     belongs to the canonical ticket;\n  2. mark the criterion `[operator-attested]` and document the evidence — this would be a\n     FALSE attestation that the defect no longer reproduces.\n\nNeither is right, and the one action that works — adding the link — is never mentioned.\nObserved on bug 9b70: the close failed repeatedly and was nearly escalated for a gate\nchange or a `--force`. The actual fix was one command, `rebar link 9b70 6a81 duplicates`,\nafter which the close passed unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] When `close_class` is in `_NON_COMPLETION_BUG_CLASSES` and NO live replacement link\n      exists, the close fails with a message naming that specific cause and the\n      `rebar link <id> <canonical> duplicates` remedy — instead of falling through to the\n      generic completion verifier's 'unmet criteria' text.\n- [ ] The check is cheap and runs BEFORE the billable LLM call (it is pure reduced-state\n      reading), so a duplicate close never spends an LLM request to produce the wrong advice.\n- [ ] A stale/dead replacement target is distinguished from a missing one — 'the ticket you\n      named is archived/deleted' is a different remedy from 'you named none'.\n- [ ] Held-out test: a bug closed `--class duplicate` with no link gets the link-specific\n      error; the same close after linking passes with no other change.\n\n## Provenance\nFound closing 9b70 (itself a duplicate of 6a81). Cross-referenced there.","id":"c8fd-1274-bcea-408e","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Close gate does not tell a duplicate close it needs a replacement link"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786380964181942001,"uuid":"cfda46b7-387d-4111-8134-2c55b109ba71"}